id: pm-vcs-47zn
title: Stat cache skips stable paths and hashes metadata changes or racy timestamps
description: "Raised in review: status called readWorkingFile and hashed every indexed file on every invocation, so its cost grew with total tracked bytes rather than with changed files. Record size, mtime, ctime, device, inode, and observation time in a versioned index; skip content only when both cached and current observations are outside the conservative timestamp window and every identity field matches. Any metadata change or racy observation falls back to content hashing, because trusting an inconclusive timestamp is how a version control system loses a same-size change."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T07:35:09.591Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T05:27:53.784Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T04:02:50.391Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T04:02:50.391Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: status on a large repository does not read file content for paths whose size and mtime are unchanged; a change made within one mtime granularity tick is still detected; the index format change is forward and backward compatible or refuses loudly
resolution: Implemented a versioned six-field filesystem identity cache with conservative racy-timestamp fallback and backward-compatible legacy reads.
expected_result: Stable indexed paths avoid content reads while metadata changes and timestamp races remain content-verified.
actual_result: Installed-CLI acceptance skipped every stable content read across 16 MiB and detected a same-size edit with restored mtime; 352 tests retain complete coverage.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-b7cb,parent,"2026-07-31T07:35:11.720Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
notes[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T04:02:03.256Z",codex,"TDD exposed a real same-timestamp false-clean failure in existing merge tests. The final design records size, mtime, ctime, device, inode, and observation time; it never trusts entries observed inside the one-second filesystem timestamp window. Focused tests pass 71/71 and the full coverage gate passes at 100/100/100. Installed pm 2026.7.31 acceptance used 64 indexed files totaling 16 MiB: strace observed zero content opens on clean cached status, and a same-size edit with restored mtime was reported modified. The exact temporary workspace was deleted afterward. The same run discovered the separate native TOON record failure now tracked as pm-vcs-l8jv."
  "2026-08-01T04:11:17.666Z",codex,"The first strict coverage run failed closed at 99.90 percent lines and 99.42 percent branches, naming the untested v2 decoder refusals and cache-state arms. Added direct corrupt-index, legacy blank-line, stable-read, and repository cached-stage tests without changing the thresholds. Final coverage gate: 352 tests, 352 passed, 100.00 percent lines, 100.00 percent branches, 100.00 percent functions across all 19 source files."
  "2026-08-01T04:25:45.870Z",codex,"CodeRabbit review identified two correctness gaps: v2 decoding rejected signed pre-epoch timestamps that the encoder can write, and the restored-mtime regression fixture stopped at the racy guard before exercising ctime comparison. Signed timestamp decoding, unsigned field rejection, and a non-racy ctime fixture now cover both paths."
  "2026-08-01T04:44:55.410Z",codex,"Cubic exact-head review tightened the cache boundary again: canonical index paths are now validated before filesystem access, both cached and current observations must be non-racy, the window covers common two-second filesystem ticks, materialization does not cache unverified concurrent bytes, and the repository-level stage test injects a failing reader to prove the bypass."
  "2026-08-01T04:52:16.831Z",codex,"The earlier Cubic head also found that a slow unchanged read beginning inside the window could finish after it yet fail to cache. Split stable identity comparison from cache trust: readWorkingFile now verifies before/after identity but bases cache eligibility on the final observation, while index reuse still requires both cached and current observations to be non-racy."
  "2026-08-01T05:07:49.374Z",codex,"Final Cubic review replaced mixed wall/filesystem age arithmetic with monotonic elapsed time between the cached and current observations. Cache entries remain unusable until two monotonic seconds have elapsed, and a reboot or clock reset that moves the current value behind the stored value fails safe. Canonical path rejection now applies at explicit normalization, working-tree discovery, encoding, and decoding, including POSIX backslashes."
  "2026-08-01T05:13:50.269Z",codex,"Final verification after raw-object and monotonic-clock fixes: 358 tests passed with 100.00 percent line, branch, and function coverage across all 19 shipped source files. Production audit found zero vulnerabilities, package dry-run succeeded, and changelog check passed."
  "2026-08-01T05:25:21.359Z",codex,"Latest Cubic review restored cross-process wall-clock observations but retained two independent safety conditions: the cached observation must be at least two seconds newer than the file metadata it verified, and the current observation must be another two seconds newer than the cache. A constructed coarse-tick regression proves a cache observed inside the tick remains unusable forever even after later wall time advances. Windows host separators are normalized before the portability rejection, while POSIX backslash filenames fail before index serialization."
  "2026-08-01T05:27:53.738Z",codex,"Coverage after the cross-process/coarse-tick reconciliation remains 100.00 percent for lines, branches, and functions across all 19 shipped source files. The suite now includes the empty-repository privacy case in addition to raw reachable/unreachable/replacement/malformed coverage."
